Guidance for Claude Code (and other agents) working in **{{ app_slug }}**, a
tenant service of a shared k3s cluster.

## What this repo is

One service, deployed by **Flux**. Everything under `kubernetes/flux/` is
reconciled into the `{{ app_namespace }}` namespace on merge to `main`; there is
no `kubectl apply` / `helm upgrade` in the normal workflow.

CI shape is **`{{ ci_shape }}`**{% if ci_shape == 'gitlab_selfhosted' %}: every job in `.gitlab-ci.yml` is included from
`{{ lib_project }}` at a pinned tag. Do not re-inline one; change behaviour by
bumping the `ref:` or adjusting the `inputs:`{% elif ci_shape == 'github' %}: `.github/workflows/` is a vendored copy of
the shared library's workflows. Keep it byte-identical to the library and
re-vendor on a bump — do not hand-edit a job{% else %}: there is no pipeline. `task lint` and the
pre-commit hooks are the whole gate{% endif %}.

The repo was generated from a copier template and records its answers in
`.copier-answers.yml`. Structural changes — enabling an HPA, an internal route,
metrics — are `copier update` with the answer flipped, not hand-assembly.

## Hard rules

- **Never push to `main`.** Every change ships via a branch +
  {{ change_request }}, even one-liners.
- **Never `kubectl apply` / `helm upgrade` to deploy.** Flux reverts drift.
  Preview with `kustomize build kubernetes/flux`; deploy by merging.
- **Never commit secrets.**
{%- if secrets_backend == 'none' %}
  This repo has no secret backend; if it grows one, it holds an `ExternalSecret`
  reference and never a value.
{%- else %}
  Values live in the `{{ secrets_backend }}` backend; this repo holds only the
  `ExternalSecret` referencing it.
{%- endif %}
- **Stay in namespace `{{ app_namespace }}`.** The Flux service account is
  RBAC-scoped to it; a manifest targeting another namespace fails to apply.
- **No `latest`/floating image tags, no privileged or root containers.** The
  namespace enforces Pod Security Admission `baseline` and warns on
  `restricted`: keep `runAsNonRoot`, dropped capabilities and a read-only root
  filesystem.
- **Register every new manifest** in `kubernetes/flux/kustomization.yaml`.
- **Run `task lint` before opening a {{ change_request }}.**

